# Okurikan (declaring ankan on a quad that does not use the just-drawn tile) is illegal after riichi
# (rules.md §1 riichi_ankan_rule, §4 item 14).
# Seat 0 holds 1111m 23m 234p 678p 8p (tenpai tanki on 8p: 111m 123m 234p 678p + 8p),
# declares double riichi and discards 9m.
# Seats 1, 2, 3 tsumogiri.
# On Seat 0's next draw, Seat 0 draws 9s (NOT 1m) while holding four 1m ->
#   assert_illegal 0: ankan:1m, assert_illegal 0: ankan!
# Seat 0 tsumogiris 9s; Seat 1 draws and discards 8p -> Seat 0 rons 8p!
# Scoring for Seat 0 (dealer, East):
#   Hand: 111m 123m 234p 678p 8p + ron 8p (dora ind 1z, ura ind 1z -> 0 dora)
#   Yaku: double_riichi (2)
#   Fu: 20 base + 10 menzen ron + 8 closed terminal triplet (111m) + 2 tanki (8p) = 40 fu
#   Dealer 2 han 40 fu ron = 3900 from Seat 1 (recovers own 1000 stick -> net +3900).

[meta]
name: riichi_ankan_okurikan_illegal
title: Okurikan (closed kan not using the just-drawn tile) is illegal after riichi
rules: mahjongsoul
source: rules.md §1, §4.14

[round]
